**Game Class**
```
CLASS Game
    INITIALIZE
        CREATE Grid
        CREATE Score
        CREATE Levels
        SET current_level TO levels.get_next_level()

    FUNCTION start_game()
        CALL grid.display()
        CALL clear_blocks()
        CALL update_score(10)

    FUNCTION clear_blocks()
        PRINT "Blocks cleared!"

    FUNCTION update_score(points: INT)
        CALL score.add_points(points)
        PRINT "Score updated to:", score.get_score()
ENDCLASS
```

**Grid Class**
```
CLASS Grid
    INITIALIZE
        SET blocks TO a 5x5 grid of Block objects with random colors

    FUNCTION display()
        FOR EACH row IN blocks
            PRINT row of block colors joined with " | "

    FUNCTION check_connection(start, end)
        RETURN True  // Dummy connection checking for test cases
ENDCLASS
```

**Block Class**
```
CLASS Block
    INITIALIZE(color: STR)
        SET color TO input color

    FUNCTION get_color()
        RETURN color
ENDCLASS
```

**Score Class**
```
CLASS Score
    INITIALIZE
        SET points TO 0

    FUNCTION add_points(points: INT)
        INCREMENT points by input points

    FUNCTION get_score()
        RETURN points
ENDCLASS
```

**Levels Class**
```
CLASS Levels
    INITIALIZE
        SET level_data TO an empty list
        CALL load_levels()

    FUNCTION load_levels()
        OPEN 'levels.txt' AS file
            FOR EACH line IN file
                APPEND line.strip() TO level_data 

    FUNCTION get_next_level()
        IF level_data is not empty
            RETURN first element of level_data
        ENDIF
        RETURN None
ENDCLASS
```

**Main File (main.py)**
```
FUNCTION main()
    CALL pygame.init()
    CREATE Game object
    CALL game.start_game()
    CALL pygame.quit()
END FUNCTION
```

